ts that were made by pfizer for  example in selling vaccines to brazil  and they emailed and they sent letters  and they offered and they called for  meetings and the government would just  not respond  pressure built on the government enough  that they had to buy vaccines but we  took so long to buy the vaccines that  once they decided to buy the answer we  got from companies is well from july on  i can give you the shots you want but i  don't have them right now because i  already sold them  brazil's limited supply of vaccines  barely makes a dent in infection rates  allowing the pandemic to rage on almost  unabated for months  when it comes to buying vaccines  you have to rush a lot of the countries  that waited  ended up having to wait longer to get  the shots  in terms of vaccination at the beginning  of the year there were no prospects as  yet on supply of the vaccines to to  africa and what was available was being  booked by the rich nations  so there was a concern that the poor  nations or low-income nations would not  get access to these vaccines at all  so kovacs was a deliberate  initiative to really ensure that there  was access to the kovind 19 vaccines  equitably among nations  kovacs founded by the who and other  global health organizations in 2020 sets  an ambitious goal for 2021  deliver nearly 2 billion vaccine doses  to low-income countries by the end of  the year  it's so important to try and get these  products into every country and every  environment  to stop this this crisis save lives as  rapidly as possible it's impossible that  the global economy going again unless  all countries are vaccinating it's  impossible to protect against the  emergence of variants if we are only  vaccinating in some parts of the world  key to kovacs's supply is a country long  known as one of the world's  pharmaceutical powerhouses  india of course is known as the pharmacy  to the world because it produces the  vast majority of the world's vaccines in  fact much 